            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of decompensating strabismic who had diplopia and vertex headaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1557-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 26-year-old female was referred for treatment who presented possible retrobulbar optic atrophy, reduced visual acuity, an LXT, a diplopia, and vertex headaches. Fresnel prisms, the simplest and most logical treatment choice were used to relieve the complaints of diplopia and vertex headaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
